          "text": "Typography is the craft of endowing human language with a durable visual form. It exists to honor content, and a page set with care invites the reader in and keeps them reading.\nThe best type does not call attention to itself. Letters sit evenly on the line, words keep a steady rhythm, and the eye moves from one line to the next without effort or doubt.\nA good body face holds up at small sizes and over long passages. Its spacing is even, its figures line up, and its italic and bold follow the voice of the text rather than shouting over it.",
